-- WHAT IS IN THE BUILDING
--
-- Everything that stands somewhere and can be looked at, talked to, or picked up.
--
-- Each one is a line with its parts divided by an upright bar:
--
--     name | shape | what it says | what it wants | what it hands over
--
-- Wanting nothing and handing nothing over makes a thing scenery. Handing something over while
-- wanting nothing makes it something you can simply take. Wanting something and handing something
-- over makes it a swap. Wanting something and handing nothing over makes it the end of the errand.
--
-- None of it relates to any of the rest of it. That is the arrangement here.


please define the folk:
    remember folk is an empty list
    add "your own front door|door|It is your front door. From this side it is a door. From the other side the neighbours insist it is a lake. You have stopped arguing about it.||" to folk
    add "a chair that is sorry|chair|The chair is sorry. It will not say what for, and you have decided not to press it.||" to folk
    add "a second moon, indoors|moon|There is a second moon in your flat, about the size of a dinner plate, hanging at shoulder height. It has been there since Thursday. You no longer mention it to people.||" to folk
    add "a man who is legally a staircase|person|Morning, says the man who is legally a staircase. Mind how you go on me. I am not insured for people who are in a hurry.||" to folk
    add "a wet floor sign|sign|The wet floor sign reads: SORRY. THE FLOOR IS DRY. WE ARE LOOKING INTO IT.||" to folk
    add "a pigeon|bird|The pigeon has an apology. Written down and signed and everything. A hat, says the pigeon. Bring me a hat and the apology is yours. I have heard a great deal about hats.|a hat|an apology" to folk
    add "a door marked NOT A DOOR|door|A door. On it, in official lettering: NOT A DOOR. It is locked, which does rather settle the argument.||" to folk
    add "a vending machine|machine|The machine sells Tuesdays. One apology each. A note taped to the glass says EXACT APOLOGY ONLY.|an apology|a Tuesday" to folk
    add "a fire extinguisher in a hat|hat|A fire extinguisher wearing a small hat. A sign beside it says DO NOT WEAR. It does not say which of the two.||a hat" to folk
    add "the Department of Slightly Wrong Things|sign|A desk, unstaffed, under a sign reading DEPARTMENT OF SLIGHTLY WRONG THINGS. There is a bell. Beside the bell: PLEASE DO NOT RING THE BELL, IT IS SLIGHTLY WRONG.||" to folk
    add "a queue of one person|queue|A queue of one person, who is not queuing for anything and would rather you did not join.||" to folk
    add "the Librarian|person|The book, says the Librarian, without looking up. Yes. I cannot take it back from you. You are not holding a Tuesday. Nobody returns a book except on a Tuesday. It is not one. You will have to bring me one.|a Tuesday|" to folk
    add "the returns slot|slot|A slot in the wall marked RETURNS. It is exactly the width of your book and roughly a mile deep.||" to folk
    give back folk
thank you for defining


